
# Analysis with Wireshark 🔍📡

Welcome to the **Analysis with Wireshark** repository! This project serves as a practical, hands-on resource hub and learning guide for mastering network packet analysis, traffic inspection, and protocol troubleshooting using Wireshark.

---

## 🎯 Overview

Wireshark is the industry-standard network protocol analyzer. This repository contains structured modules, analysis workflows, capture files (`.pcap` / `.pcapng`), and display filter cheat sheets designed to help you dissect live network traffic and identify performance bottlenecks or security threats.

---

## 📌 Key Objectives

* **Packet Inspection:** Understand OSI and TCP/IP layer dynamics through deep packet analysis.
* **Filtering Mastery:** Apply advanced capture and display filters to isolate relevant traffic.
* **Stream Reconstruction:** Reconstruct network conversations across protocols (TCP, HTTP, DNS, TLS).
* **Performance Troubleshooting:** Identify latency, packet loss, TCP retransmissions, and window scale issues.
* **Security Analysis:** Detect network anomalies, port scans, unencrypted credential exposure, and suspicious payloads.

---

## 📂 Repository Structure

* **`01-fundamentals/`** — Getting started with Wireshark, interface setup, and basic display filters.
* **`02-core-protocols/`** — In-depth inspection of ARP, IP, ICMP, TCP handshakes, DNS, and HTTP/HTTPS.
* **`03-network-troubleshooting/`** — Real-world scenarios on diagnosing network lag, dropped packets, and bad performance.
* **`04-security-and-forensics/`** — Analyzing malware C2 communications, spoofing attacks, and rogue traffic.
* **`pcaps/`** — Sample packet capture files used for hands-on exercises.

---

## 🛠️ Prerequisites

* Basic understanding of networking fundamentals (TCP/IP model, IP addressing, ports, and protocols).
* Wireshark installed on your machine ([Download Wireshark](https://www.wireshark.org/download.html)).
